WEBVTT

00:00:58.069 --> 00:01:00.319
And they got fabulously
wealthy in doing so.

00:01:00.343 --> 00:01:02.676
And they built beautiful cities

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.800
all powered on that coal.

00:01:07.612 --> 00:01:11.033
And back here in the United States,

00:01:11.057 --> 00:01:13.204
we saw economic despair, deprivation.

00:01:13.228 --> 00:01:14.676
This is what I saw.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.331
I saw people struggling to get by,

00:01:17.355 --> 00:01:20.450
not knowing what was what
and what was next.

00:01:20.474 --> 00:01:22.741
And I asked myself the question:

00:01:22.765 --> 00:01:26.095
How is it possible that we could
be so poor here in the United States,

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.824
because coal is such a wealthy
resource; it's so much money?

00:01:29.848 --> 00:01:31.008
And I realize: